{:edb/db-before-t 1890 :edb/db-after-t 1891 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535203 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:27:43.801Z" 13194139535203 true] [17592186096560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337318 13194139535203 true] [17592186096560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337325 13194139535203 true] [17592186096671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337308 13194139535203 true] [17592186096671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337315 13194139535203 true] [17592186096671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337332 13194139535203 true] [17592186337308 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337309 13194139535203 true] [17592186337308 1089 "q-10032" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337308 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535203 true] [17592186337308 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/assets/9e19c1cd8bca76f1eec39acfa1b09c0f08b67faea5ddce8325e093923d21d394.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x+1},$ the $y$-axis and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." 13194139535203 true] [17592186337308 1113 #uuid "a2c8f25f-d60e-58d8-adfc-09591d2ab6e3" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337308 1145 "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{x+1} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =x+1 \\\\ x & ={y}^{3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}-y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-0)-(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $|-\\frac{3}{4}|=\\frac{3}{4}.$" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337310 13194139535203 true] [17592186337309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337311 13194139535203 true] [17592186337309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337312 13194139535203 true] [17592186337309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337313 13194139535203 true] [17592186337309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337314 13194139535203 true] [17592186337309 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535203 true] [17592186337309 1041 "selection" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337309 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337313 13194139535203 true] [17592186337309 1110 #uuid "6ac910ea-ce2f-5316-b11e-358af9b1341b" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337310 1034 "-\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337310 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337310 1111 #uuid "5a6007b2-1915-5162-b380-0c13e4581369" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337311 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337311 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337311 1111 #uuid "db68eb30-cb54-5370-99c0-6b8de6320155" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337312 1034 "1" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337312 1111 #uuid "2a2a01ef-7dea-584e-a566-a6af37e1fbf2" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337313 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337313 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337313 1111 #uuid "0c4163d9-ef06-55ee-9099-c216494d24ff" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337314 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337314 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337314 1111 #uuid "28fe86e6-f058-5fb2-9698-01fc50401b95" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337315 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337316 13194139535203 true] [17592186337315 1089 "q-346783" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337315 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535203 true] [17592186337315 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/assets/816b36f644f3e41d8f48bed2dd49e150d751cb13e082b6a1b9b4ad16973d3d57.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ between the curve $y=3\\sqrt{\\frac{x+3}{3}}$, the $y$-axis and the lines $y=1$ and $y=2,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337315 1113 #uuid "c61a2e55-9279-560a-a21e-c4a0618f9e54" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337315 1145 "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\sqrt{\\frac{x+3}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{x+3}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =\\frac{x+3}{3} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =x+3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-3)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}\\,|}_{1}^{2}-3\\cdot y\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})-3(2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}-3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So, the area that we want is\n\n$$\nA=|-\\frac{20}{9}|=\\frac{20}{9}\\,.\n$$" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337316 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337317 13194139535203 true] [17592186337316 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535203 true] [17592186337316 1041 "field-1" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337316 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337317 13194139535203 true] [17592186337316 1110 #uuid "eb364830-507a-582d-82ce-38cf323a5600" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337317 1034 "\\frac{20}{9}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337317 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337317 1111 #uuid "8500aa29-4719-5c4c-a3ca-f35c6ede931f" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337318 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337319 13194139535203 true] [17592186337318 1089 "q-78888" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337318 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535203 true] [17592186337318 1100 "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $x=16{y}^{4}-1$ and the $y$-axis." 13194139535203 true] [17592186337318 1113 #uuid "94aef3ce-716b-5bd0-a343-fed185ba9a2e" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337318 1145 "First, we find $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{y}^{4}-1 & =0 \\\\ 16{y}^{4} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{4} & =\\frac{1}{16} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/assets/c1e092dd6302bb5948c6452e43b093fc3a531132580c1bb1e42fbe846152f63c.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=16{y}^{4}-1$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ to $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}(16{y}^{4}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}(16{y}^{4}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =32{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y-2{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =32\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}|}_{0}^{1/2}-2\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}(\\frac{1}{32}-0)-2(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $|-\\frac{4}{5}|=\\frac{4}{5}.$" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337319 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337320 13194139535203 true] [17592186337319 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337321 13194139535203 true] [17592186337319 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337322 13194139535203 true] [17592186337319 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337323 13194139535203 true] [17592186337319 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337324 13194139535203 true] [17592186337319 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535203 true] [17592186337319 1041 "selection" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337319 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337322 13194139535203 true] [17592186337319 1110 #uuid "92143d1e-75a1-5e86-90e1-1ec3bf84ab21" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337320 1034 "\\frac{3}{10}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337320 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337320 1111 #uuid "8a23a8f4-deb3-5a57-95f0-17ad16d1eac0" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337321 1034 "\\frac{7}{5}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337321 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337321 1111 #uuid "6ed6ddb7-d571-5dd3-83ae-8a4ab24d7a51" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337322 1034 "\\frac{4}{5}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337322 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337322 1111 #uuid "392b5bf6-ac20-51cc-a18b-aa3d9ed320c0" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337323 1034 "\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337323 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337323 1111 #uuid "2b29bad7-a690-5677-a992-4dce2b94dc81" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337324 1034 "\\frac{7}{10}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337324 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337324 1111 #uuid "63b6008d-355a-5d97-bf38-fe33df8a1f5a" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337325 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337326 13194139535203 true] [17592186337325 1089 "q-78891" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337325 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535203 true] [17592186337325 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/assets/a45999ec28d309b3be249304e9b5175f66f2b862cd7f18f2c51b3182333e9a08.png)\n\nFind the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and the $y$-axis, as shown above." 13194139535203 true] [17592186337325 1113 #uuid "395038c5-fc04-5903-a4d5-851b4cfb7b17" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337325 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =0 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that we want to find the area between the curve $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ to $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =4(1-0) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337327 13194139535203 true] [17592186337326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337328 13194139535203 true] [17592186337326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337329 13194139535203 true] [17592186337326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337330 13194139535203 true] [17592186337326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337331 13194139535203 true] [17592186337326 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535203 true] [17592186337326 1041 "selection" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337326 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337331 13194139535203 true] [17592186337326 1110 #uuid "9415b612-7882-5f74-b7c4-26c49630918d" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337327 1034 "3" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337327 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337327 1111 #uuid "b87da0b6-309e-5f28-b180-65f154632e45" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337328 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337328 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337328 1111 #uuid "72ddbc94-0650-5233-8dec-b9fffd42d3be" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337329 1034 "2" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337329 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337329 1111 #uuid "c35d5824-5a15-5158-ab70-a59a2f17ded4" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337330 1034 "\\pi " 13194139535203 true] [17592186337330 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186337330 1111 #uuid "3ff44da7-7f0b-5e31-adc9-2482cc0ee02a" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337331 1034 "4" 13194139535203 true] [17592186337331 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535203 true] [17592186